        "original_id": "9d4c1bba-45b6-565f-97af-4de448ed622c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Audra McDonald, Harold Arlen, Adam Guettel, Elena Shaddow, Katie Clarke, Victoria Clark\n- Works: How Glory Goes, The Light in the Piazza\n- Awards: Tony Award for Best Leading Actress in a Musical\n\nFacts:\n- Adam Guettel was born on December 16, 1964, and he is an American composer-lyricist of musical theater and opera.\n- How Glory Goes is Audra McDonald’s second album, and it was released in 2000.\n- Five songs on How Glory Goes were written by Harold Arlen.\n- Two songs on How Glory Goes were written by Adam Guettel, including the title track.\n- In 2005, Victoria Clark won the Tony Award for Best Leading Actress in a Musical for her role in The Light in the Piazza.\n- Elena Shaddow recently toured as Clara Johnson in Adam Guettel’s The Light in the Piazza before leaving the production and being replaced by Katie Clarke.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
